   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Sudhir,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for sharing your results. In my opinion you got an amazing result 148 in 150. </div><div><br></div><div>It happens because sometime two plants are too close and touching each other and the algorithm doesn&#39;t recognize as two different objects. Also, when you use minSize=0.8 you are eliminating the really small plant in your second line (maybe you should to use 0.7 or 0.5 and see if it can control this problem)</div><div><br></div><div>FIELDimageR uses image segmentation approaches. The quality of your analysis will depends of your image quality (for example, taking pictures in early stages and avoiding plants touching each other). </div><div><br></div><div>Another solution is to try play around with the fieldMask (changing indices) and chose another index to help you split better your plants.</div><div><br></div><div>Let me know if you fixed it, but again your results are impressive due to evaluating late plants (touching each other).</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Filipe Matias</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
